1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,980
Amen.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:50,020
Well, good morning, everyone.

3
00:00:50,020 --> 00:00:59,360
It's going to take probably just a few minutes for us to rein in the, uh, whatever that is happening in my ear.

4
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:00,180
But we'll figure it out.

5
00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:06,940
Don't think I didn't notice that those of you with, uh, teams whose jerseys with teams who aren't that good.

6
00:01:06,940 --> 00:01:10,400
You guys were more pumped.

7
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:13,480
You were like, yeah, of course we should yell for Jesus more than our football team.

8
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:14,060
I saw it.

9
00:01:14,060 --> 00:01:15,340
I saw it.

10
00:01:15,340 --> 00:01:15,820
I'm just kidding.

11
00:01:15,820 --> 00:01:21,180
For those of you who haven't met me yet or I haven't got to meet you yet, I'm looking forward to that day.

12
00:01:21,180 --> 00:01:21,960
My name is Ryan.

13
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:23,380
I'm one of the pastors here.

14
00:01:23,380 --> 00:01:28,020
And just an honor, seriously, an honor and a privilege to be a part of this community.

15
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:30,980
That we call Canvas Community Church.

16
00:01:30,980 --> 00:01:32,260
God has been so good to us.

17
00:01:32,260 --> 00:01:34,140
And you all are wonderful people.

18
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:38,180
Chasing after Jesus with, with all of yourselves.

19
00:01:38,180 --> 00:01:41,340
And so excited to be here launching a new series.

20
00:01:41,340 --> 00:01:44,920
Uh, it's going to be a longer series, community and service.

21
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:50,740
It's a part of our three-year, nine-part series on practice-based discipleship.

22
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:55,820
So if you're newer, you might not have caught any of our practice-based discipleship curriculum.

23
00:01:55,820 --> 00:01:58,880
It's through an organization called Practicing the Way.

24
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:05,080
And really, it's built on nine practices that we can pull out from the life and teachings of Jesus.

25
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:08,520
And the theory is, and I don't think it's a theory.

26
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:21,000
I think it's just true, is that discipleship in the Western church, discipleship in America, often centers around information and knowledge before obedience.

27
00:02:22,140 --> 00:02:27,260
And we often like to talk about people who are mature in the faith because they know a lot of Bible.

28
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:36,320
But the whole idea about these, this practice-based discipleship is that maturity in discipleship to Jesus is obedience to Jesus.

29
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:45,120
And yes, we should increase our understanding, our knowledge about the Scriptures that Jesus called his Bible, the Old Testament, the Jewish Bible.

30
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:50,520
And yes, we should do our best to understand the New Testament teachings in their context.

31
00:02:50,520 --> 00:03:01,080
But if we spend so much time and energy, if all of our Bible studies, all of our meetings, all of our gatherings about filling our head with information that we do nothing about,

32
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:06,840
then the Scripture rebukes us as those who are hearers of the word but not doers.

33
00:03:06,840 --> 00:03:16,320
And so we really, as a church, we want to hone in on this idea of we're going to talk about the Scriptures and then we're going to live them out.

34
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:26,640
And if we get so focused on just more information, more knowledge, but we don't have love, we've missed the point.

35
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:41,020
And there's nothing more heartbreaking for me as a pastor than having somebody set a meeting with me to have a conversation about the nuances of very, very niche theology and what I believe.

36
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:48,640
And then, like, you look and it's like, that's all they care about is the nuances of theology and not loving their neighbor as their self.

37
00:03:48,640 --> 00:03:52,720
And it's a trap that all of us can fall into.

38
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:54,580
It's a trap that I fall into on a regular basis.

39
00:03:54,580 --> 00:04:00,140
So I'm not here to condemn as much as I am to just like, let's keep this before us on a regular basis.

40
00:04:00,140 --> 00:04:04,840
So far, the practices that we've covered are prayer, fasting, generosity, and solitude.

41
00:04:06,060 --> 00:04:09,800
And if you didn't get any of those and you want those, they're all on our website.

42
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:10,760
You can check those out.

43
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:15,200
As we head into the next series, we're going to do community and service together.

44
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:17,060
These are best done in small groups.

45
00:04:17,060 --> 00:04:20,740
Those don't have to be small groups that are sponsored by our church.

46
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:24,240
We do as many small groups as we can to create space for all of you.

47
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:32,520
But if you just want to find a neighbor, find a friend, find another follower of Jesus, and you want to get together with them and talk about these things and live them out together, that's wonderful.

48
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:36,160
There are a couple of new small groups that are launching.

49
00:04:36,160 --> 00:04:42,620
New small groups are always great for those of you that haven't been in one because you don't feel like you're hopping into a group of people that already know each other really well.

50
00:04:42,620 --> 00:04:49,260
So like Corey said, there are going to be two, at least two this week and then more next week of new groups.

51
00:04:49,260 --> 00:04:50,240
I think there might even be three.

52
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:52,040
Lisa, are you planning on heading back there as well?

53
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:53,020
I didn't talk to you beforehand.

54
00:04:53,620 --> 00:04:55,420
But yeah, so there's new groups.

55
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:58,360
These are awesome opportunities to get plugged into.

56
00:04:58,360 --> 00:05:07,960
And my ultimate desire is that all of our small groups who are meeting together to cultivate community will work together at the end of this to plan a service project.

57
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:10,220
Do something together.

58
00:05:10,220 --> 00:05:12,720
Your community that you're forming, do some type of service.

59
00:05:12,720 --> 00:05:17,860
And if all of that goes well, the last Sunday of this series, I'd like to just be a testimony Sunday.

60
00:05:18,300 --> 00:05:27,300
A Sunday where our groups come up and share what God has been doing through them getting outside of themselves to serve their neighbors and those who are in need.

61
00:05:27,300 --> 00:05:29,280
So that's kind of the overarching goal.

62
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:34,140
Technically, an eight-week series that I turned into a 10-week series because why not, right?

63
00:05:35,420 --> 00:05:40,040
So this Sunday, we're kind of going to set the stage for how community and service are together.

64
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:45,120
And then we're going to take a break on the 28th for our Celebration Sunday.

65
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:51,780
It's cool because the week before our Celebration Sunday, the theme is to share your joys and sorrows together in your community.

66
00:05:52,160 --> 00:06:03,040
So we're going to pause and take a Sunday to really share the joy of what God has done in our church that has merged two churches together and started a brand new thing three years ago.

67
00:06:03,040 --> 00:06:04,100
We're going to celebrate that.

68
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:05,800
We're going to honor one another.

69
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:09,000
More details about that are coming.

70
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:14,180
I just want to warn you, it's going to be chaotic and beautiful.

71
00:06:15,140 --> 00:06:22,240
So one of the things we're going to do is we want to highlight, we want to honor our volunteers who partner with God to make this stuff happen.

72
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:33,440
And so what's on the chopping block, what's on the plans in dark pencil is no children's ministry for a Sunday.

73
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:34,700
It's going to be awesome.

74
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:35,920
We did the math on the chairs.

75
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:37,100
I know it looks full in here.

76
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:40,720
My phrase that I'm telling you is embrace the chaos.

77
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:42,420
It's going to be beautiful.

78
00:06:42,420 --> 00:06:43,780
We're going to open up the double doors.

79
00:06:43,780 --> 00:06:45,020
We're going to have chairs out in the lobby.

80
00:06:45,140 --> 00:06:51,100
We're going to set up strategic spaces for if you have a fussy kid that you're insecure about, you want to take them to play, that's totally fine.

81
00:06:51,100 --> 00:06:57,540
But just know we're not going to be bothered by kids being kids because we're family, we're community.

82
00:06:57,540 --> 00:07:00,240
So that's the plan for now.

83
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:02,000
I think we've got a donut truck.

84
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,500
I think we've got the playground at the kids club.

85
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:06,780
Lots of cool things that are going to happen that Sunday.

86
00:07:06,780 --> 00:07:08,980
So if you can make it, we'd love for you to be there.

87
00:07:08,980 --> 00:07:13,120
If you have crippling anxiety in crowds, you probably don't come here already.

88
00:07:14,220 --> 00:07:22,920
But if you do, you might want to just kind of plan ahead and think of all of the exits that you can get out if it gets overwhelming.

89
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:24,920
But we love you guys.

90
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:25,620
We love all of you.

91
00:07:25,620 --> 00:07:27,700
So, all right, let's pray and we'll hop in.

92
00:07:29,380 --> 00:07:41,180
Oh, Father in heaven, Abba, you have brought us into a family through the death, burial, resurrection, and ascension of Jesus.

93
00:07:41,180 --> 00:07:50,120
And that is not a family that we should think about, a group that we just get together with once every two and a half weeks on a Sunday morning for an hour.

94
00:07:50,220 --> 00:07:51,420
God, this is family.

95
00:07:51,420 --> 00:08:00,320
We are brothers and sisters, mothers and fathers, aunts and uncles, children, all under you as our Abba.

96
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:04,440
God, we want to live into that vision more clearly.

97
00:08:05,640 --> 00:08:08,180
We want to be family around the table with one another.

98
00:08:08,180 --> 00:08:23,560
And we don't want that just to be for our good, but we want that to be for the good of the community around us who is searching, looking, grasping for anything they can to fill the void in their life, which is being loved by an eternally loving father.

99
00:08:24,020 --> 00:08:29,280
We want to go out with that love and serve our community and share the good news of Jesus with them.

100
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:32,300
And so, God, may that be our posture for the next 10 weeks.

101
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:42,360
May we prepare our hearts and our minds and our schedules to invest in one another so that we can go out and serve those who are in need in our community.

102
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:44,840
It's in Jesus' name I pray.

103
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:45,600
Amen.

104
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:50,960
If you have a Bible and you want to follow along with me, we're going to be in Titus chapter 2.

105
00:08:51,360 --> 00:08:56,520
I know all of you spend a lot of time in the book of Titus, so you should know exactly where we're headed.

106
00:08:56,520 --> 00:09:04,140
Last week, we finished up our psalm series, and we wrapped it up with a message on Christian unity.

107
00:09:04,140 --> 00:09:15,420
And I said, and you all, yes and amen to the fact that we live in a current cultural moment where people are busy, isolated, disconnected, and divided.

108
00:09:15,420 --> 00:09:17,100
Can we yes and amen that again?

109
00:09:18,260 --> 00:09:27,020
This is the air that we breathe, is this unhealthy culture where most of us are so busy, and that leads us to be isolated and disconnected.

110
00:09:27,020 --> 00:09:32,800
And that disconnection leads us to become divided from our brothers and sisters in unhealthy ways.

111
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:41,660
We said that God is inviting his people to live into a unified Christian community that can be a countercultural witness to the world around us.

112
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:42,360
Do we remember this?

113
00:09:42,360 --> 00:09:45,120
Thank you.

114
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:45,780
Thank you.

115
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:48,860
I know sometimes I ask questions, and you're like, does he actually want me to answer that or not?

116
00:09:48,860 --> 00:09:50,680
So I gave you time, and you did it.

117
00:09:50,680 --> 00:09:51,520
I appreciate that.

118
00:09:53,380 --> 00:09:59,400
So my question then becomes for us, this is an inspirational message that most of us would agree with intellectually.

119
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:20,420
But if discipleship to Jesus is more than just agreeing with biblical truth, is there a practice or practices from the life of Jesus that we can intentionally build into our lives that will help us cultivate this countercultural unity that demonstrates God's kingdom on earth as it is in heaven?

120
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:23,160
Yes.

121
00:10:23,160 --> 00:10:23,220
Yes.

122
00:10:23,220 --> 00:10:24,100
Thank you, Gary.

123
00:10:24,100 --> 00:10:27,600
Community and service are on tap for the next 10 weeks.

124
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:29,000
I'm glad you asked.

125
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,600
I'm glad you shared.

126
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:34,500
It's community and service, and they are our primary countercultural practices.

127
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:41,620
Taking practical steps to intentionally live life with one another in community, and this is not easy.

128
00:10:41,620 --> 00:10:43,400
You don't fall into community.

129
00:10:43,400 --> 00:10:45,400
You have to be proactive.

130
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:47,340
You have to reorient your calendar.

131
00:10:47,340 --> 00:10:52,640
You have to be intentional with the people that Christ has called you into family with.

132
00:10:54,980 --> 00:10:58,120
And then serving God together in those communities.

133
00:10:58,120 --> 00:11:01,260
We don't form these communities solely for our own benefit.

134
00:11:01,260 --> 00:11:03,780
We remain united.

135
00:11:03,780 --> 00:11:05,400
And here's the other thing, too.

136
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:11,260
By serving alongside one another, we said that community is for all of our brothers and sisters in Christ.

137
00:11:11,580 --> 00:11:15,460
And do we naturally get along with all of our brothers and sisters in Christ?

138
00:11:15,460 --> 00:11:17,840
Wasn't that what last week was all about, right?

139
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:18,880
Like, unity is hard.

140
00:11:18,880 --> 00:11:19,840
Unity is difficult.

141
00:11:20,620 --> 00:11:34,460
But what I find is that when brothers and sisters who are in community together go out and serve those who are less fortunate, serve those who are in need, serve those who are searching for hope and healing and a future, the things that we fight over become less and less important.

142
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:44,400
It's like if we're serving a marginalized group of people outside of ourselves, the things that we fight over and get in internal battles about become less and less important.

143
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:45,660
And that increases unity.

144
00:11:45,660 --> 00:11:54,040
This is why we've tied these two things together, because we can all get around a table and have weekly conversations and get in fights about secondary theology.

145
00:11:54,040 --> 00:12:00,540
Or we could all come around a table centered on the death, burial, and resurrection of Jesus, and then we can take that hope out to the watching world.

146
00:12:00,540 --> 00:12:05,460
And maybe we won't have time to fight about little nuanced, difficult conversations, right?

147
00:12:05,460 --> 00:12:06,920
So that's the point.

148
00:12:06,920 --> 00:12:13,340
Community and service together, living as family and serving outside of ourselves.

149
00:12:13,340 --> 00:12:19,160
And the passage that we're going to look at in Titus, I think, really encapsulates this whole message.

150
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:21,800
It's a perfect passage for us to launch these practices.

151
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:34,760
Because Paul is writing this letter to Titus, a church leader that he left on the island of Crete, to help them cultivate Christian community that lives as a countercultural witness to the ungodly culture around them.

152
00:12:34,760 --> 00:12:37,680
And Crete was ungodly.

153
00:12:37,680 --> 00:12:40,580
One of their own secular prophets wrote this.

154
00:12:40,580 --> 00:12:46,660
Paul quotes it in the letter that Cretans are always liars, evil brutes, and lazy gluttons.

155
00:12:46,660 --> 00:12:48,960
Fun, right?

156
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:59,240
And the reason Paul sent Titus to Crete is because the church in Crete was not living into this vision of being a countercultural community that served others outside of themselves.

157
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:05,380
They were becoming—they had two main struggles that you can find as you read along the book.

158
00:13:05,380 --> 00:13:10,980
Some of the Cretan believers were living lives that looked no different than the culture around them.

159
00:13:10,980 --> 00:13:17,300
They were Cretan with Jesus slapped on the bumper sticker of their whatever they had, right?

160
00:13:18,160 --> 00:13:31,000
And then there was another group of people that were taking hold of leadership in the church, and they were very religious believers that were far more concerned with external obedience than they were with transformation from the inside.

161
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:37,700
Now, strict religious obedience that made the gospel inaccessible to the culture around them.

162
00:13:37,700 --> 00:13:40,060
And Paul equally rebuked both.

163
00:13:40,060 --> 00:13:41,380
See, here's the thing.

164
00:13:41,380 --> 00:13:47,400
I think church people think that one of those things is worse than the other.

165
00:13:47,400 --> 00:14:00,820
I think people that were raised in the church think that, like, nominal Christianity with no obedience and just being conformed to the culture around them is worse than religiosity inside the church.

166
00:14:00,820 --> 00:14:04,360
And, like, when I read the Scriptures, I think they both get rebuked the same.

167
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:09,600
And so if you're a church person and you're like, yeah, at least I don't look like the culture around me.

168
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:17,040
It's like, yeah, but are you being religious and making the gospel inaccessible to the people outside the walls of the church?

169
00:14:17,040 --> 00:14:19,880
Sound anything like us today?

170
00:14:19,880 --> 00:14:34,660
Apathetic towards sin and lazy in our obedience as we blend with the culture around us or self-righteously obedient to external standards while hardening our hearts to the community around us, unwilling to serve hurting people unless they play by our rules.

171
00:14:35,980 --> 00:14:54,220
So Paul's charge to Titus is to develop a tight-knit community, family around the table of faithful believers who take sin seriously and take obedience to the gospel seriously and who are willing to lay down their external religiosity to serve those among them in need.

172
00:14:55,400 --> 00:15:01,100
The passage that we're going to look at today is Paul's summary statement about this project that he sent Titus on.

173
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:16,180
Essentially what he's saying in this summary paragraph is, Titus, if you're going to succeed in this thing, cultivating a community of believers who take obedience to Jesus seriously and then go outside and serve from themselves, these are the things that you're going to have to do.

174
00:15:16,280 --> 00:15:18,000
This is the mindset that you're going to have to have.

175
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:18,560
Let's read it.

176
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:22,160
Titus chapter 2, verses 11 through 15.

177
00:15:22,160 --> 00:15:40,080
For the grace of God has appeared that offers salvation to people that look like me, people that vote like me, people in my economic status.

178
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:44,460
For the grace of God has appeared that offers salvation to all people.

179
00:15:44,460 --> 00:15:56,880
It teaches us to say no to ungodliness and worldly passions and to live self-controlled, upright, and godly lives in this present age while we wait for the blessed hope,

180
00:15:57,520 --> 00:16:08,500
the appearing of the glory of our great God and Savior, Jesus Christ, who gave himself for us to redeem us from all wickedness and to purify.

181
00:16:08,500 --> 00:16:10,880
Listen, this is the summary statement.

182
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:21,920
This is what Paul is saying, that Jesus died to purify for himself a people, a community that are his very own possession, his family, flesh and blood,

183
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:26,180
and they are eager to do what is good.

184
00:16:26,180 --> 00:16:36,420
These then are the things you should teach, encourage and rebuke with all authority and do not let anyone despise you.

185
00:16:39,900 --> 00:16:50,140
We see that summary in Paul's language, that the whole point, this whole thing, the gospel is all about Jesus redeeming for himself a community of believers

186
00:16:50,140 --> 00:16:55,600
who are eager to go outside of themselves and serve those who are struggling, those who are hurting.

187
00:16:55,600 --> 00:17:02,040
As I worked on this message today, I gotta be honest with you, I'm not necessarily proud of it, but my old Baptist roots came out a little bit.

188
00:17:03,060 --> 00:17:08,960
I couldn't help it, I've broken down this passage with three truths, all starting with the letter A.

189
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:14,160
And if you're lucky, we might even end with a poem, who knows?

190
00:17:14,160 --> 00:17:20,800
So, three truths that we need to embrace in order to pursue the practices of community and service.

191
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:24,540
Paul is telling Titus that this project of community and service is going to work.

192
00:17:24,540 --> 00:17:29,000
These are the truths that have to get inside of the believers that you are pastoring.

193
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:35,640
They have to embody these, they have to embrace these, they have to believe these, not just in their minds, but in their very souls.

194
00:17:35,640 --> 00:17:42,400
The first is this idea of adoption, adoption.

195
00:17:42,400 --> 00:17:49,140
Verse 11, for the grace of God has appeared that offers salvation to all people.

196
00:17:49,140 --> 00:17:52,100
Paul starts the summary of his argument by saying,

197
00:17:52,100 --> 00:18:03,060
The project to unite obedient followers of Jesus into community with one another who are willing to sacrificially serve outside of themselves only works if it's rooted in the grace of God.

198
00:18:03,060 --> 00:18:09,740
It only works if these people understand what God has done for them in Jesus.

199
00:18:09,740 --> 00:18:14,080
So what is this grace that has appeared?

200
00:18:14,080 --> 00:18:17,920
What is the ultimate grace of God that has appeared to the community of believers?

201
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:20,000
It is the person of Jesus Christ.

202
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:24,080
God in the flesh has appeared to his image bearers.

203
00:18:24,080 --> 00:18:29,160
He has modeled for us how to live a life in harmony with the purposes of God.

204
00:18:29,160 --> 00:18:35,960
Even in a world marred by sin, Jesus, God in the flesh, stepped into human creation, marred by sin.

205
00:18:35,960 --> 00:18:38,020
Temptation everywhere.

206
00:18:38,020 --> 00:18:42,220
Difficult situations to navigate, grace and truth everywhere.

207
00:18:42,380 --> 00:18:48,020
Surrounded by sinners and Jesus modeled for us what it looks like to live grace and truth.

208
00:18:48,020 --> 00:18:50,840
He is our example, but he is not only our example.

209
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:58,680
He died a sacrificial death, raised from the dead, ascended into heaven, making a way for people to be brought back into the family of God.

210
00:18:58,680 --> 00:19:03,740
At the heart of the grace of Jesus is the concept of adoption.

211
00:19:03,740 --> 00:19:10,260
We've been brought into a new family through the death, burial, and resurrection of Jesus.

212
00:19:11,260 --> 00:19:15,200
At the very heart of the grace of God is this concept of adoption.

213
00:19:15,200 --> 00:19:26,800
Every single one of us, every image bearer on earth was created to be in an eternally loving relationship with the creator of the universe as their Abba, their Papa.

214
00:19:26,800 --> 00:19:32,380
And each and every one of us has chosen to break that relationship.

215
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:36,300
We are all fatherless prodigals who have taken hold of God's creation.

216
00:19:37,500 --> 00:19:42,220
We have broken our relationship with him and we are using his stuff for our own personal gain.

217
00:19:45,220 --> 00:19:48,660
This is the reality of all of creation before Jesus.

218
00:19:48,660 --> 00:19:55,880
We are fatherless prodigals who have taken God's creation and are running away from him and using his stuff to accomplish our own purposes.

219
00:19:55,880 --> 00:20:02,340
And whether you realize it or not and whether you're ready to acknowledge it or not, this causes damage to you and to those around you.

220
00:20:02,340 --> 00:20:05,500
This is the sin and the effects of sin all around us.

221
00:20:05,500 --> 00:20:07,220
This is why Jesus takes sin so seriously.

222
00:20:07,380 --> 00:20:10,700
It's not because he just wants to slap us over the wrist with a bunch of rules.

223
00:20:10,700 --> 00:20:13,820
It's because when we sin, it hurts us and it hurts others.

224
00:20:18,820 --> 00:20:29,460
We're all essentially self-proclaimed eternal orphans grasping for anything to fill the void we have from our willful separation from our eternally loving father.

225
00:20:29,460 --> 00:20:38,160
And the grace of God that Paul is talking about here is the person of Christ making a way for us to be adopted into the family of God again.

226
00:20:40,540 --> 00:20:52,980
Paul is telling Titus that if he's ever going to be able to wrangle this ragtag group of disobedient and self-righteous people who claim to follow Jesus together in a unified community that serves outside themselves,

227
00:20:52,980 --> 00:20:56,340
they have to understand the grace of God that's been given to them.

228
00:20:56,340 --> 00:21:00,320
The self-righteous have to understand that they cannot earn their way back to God.

229
00:21:00,320 --> 00:21:04,080
They have to understand that it is a gift freely given to them.

230
00:21:05,540 --> 00:21:14,700
And those who claim the blood of Jesus over their lives but aren't living differently than the world around them have to realize that they are no longer orphans out on the streets,

231
00:21:14,700 --> 00:21:17,160
but they have been adopted into the family of God.

232
00:21:17,160 --> 00:21:19,660
And that comes with a new identity and a new purpose.

233
00:21:19,660 --> 00:21:24,240
We've got to live into this family.

234
00:21:24,240 --> 00:21:31,820
Not just with the ones that we like, but with all people who claim Jesus as Lord.

235
00:21:32,580 --> 00:21:38,660
Genuine Christian community begins with a deep understanding and an internalization of our adoption.

236
00:21:38,660 --> 00:21:51,400
If we're really going to take Christian community seriously, we have to realize the work of Christ was to bring all people who trust Jesus into family with one another.

237
00:21:51,400 --> 00:21:56,360
If you don't believe me, here's the words of Jesus in Matthew 12, verse 50.

238
00:21:56,360 --> 00:22:04,420
When his actual family were looking for him, people come to him and say, hey, your mom and your brothers are all looking for you.

239
00:22:04,420 --> 00:22:07,820
And he says, who are my mother and my brothers?

240
00:22:07,820 --> 00:22:09,620
My sisters, my father.

241
00:22:09,620 --> 00:22:16,840
For whoever does the will of my father in heaven is my brother and sister and mother.

242
00:22:16,840 --> 00:22:21,740
Jesus is saying adoption is at the heart of the kingdom of God.

243
00:22:21,740 --> 00:22:32,060
God, all of us become family when we obey the will of the father, when we realize that we are orphans on the run, and when we turn from that, repent and move towards God.

244
00:22:32,060 --> 00:22:38,580
When we accept the grace and forgiveness that he has given us, we become family with one another, and that is messy.

245
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:41,980
But man, is it beautiful.

246
00:22:41,980 --> 00:22:50,720
The grace of God invites us to be adopted into a new family with all those who trust and obey Jesus as Lord.

247
00:22:50,720 --> 00:22:52,520
We good with the first A?

248
00:22:52,520 --> 00:22:55,020
All right, we're moving on.

249
00:22:55,020 --> 00:22:58,440
Adoption, from adoption to alignment.

250
00:22:58,440 --> 00:23:03,120
And this one, I got to be honest with you, a bit of a stretch.

251
00:23:04,740 --> 00:23:05,940
But it started with an A.

252
00:23:05,940 --> 00:23:06,700
So we're here.

253
00:23:06,700 --> 00:23:08,100
I'll explain it.

254
00:23:08,100 --> 00:23:09,220
It'll make sense when we're done.

255
00:23:09,220 --> 00:23:11,980
But I was feeling Baptist this week.

256
00:23:11,980 --> 00:23:12,740
I don't know what to tell you.

257
00:23:12,740 --> 00:23:15,600
Alignment.

258
00:23:15,600 --> 00:23:16,900
Adoption leads to alignment.

259
00:23:16,900 --> 00:23:19,380
Verse 12, it teaches us the grace of God.

260
00:23:19,380 --> 00:23:19,920
Listen to this.

261
00:23:19,920 --> 00:23:21,740
Don't miss the connection that he's making here.

262
00:23:21,740 --> 00:23:22,660
What teaches us?

263
00:23:22,660 --> 00:23:29,960
The grace of God, this idea that we've been brought into a new family, that teaches us to say no to ungodliness and worldly passions,

264
00:23:29,960 --> 00:23:35,420
and to live self-controlled, upright, and godly lives in this present age.

265
00:23:35,420 --> 00:23:40,920
It's the grace of God revealed to us in Christ that leads us to obedience.

266
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:48,500
It's our adoption as heirs of the king of the universe that brings us into alignment or to obedience.

267
00:23:48,500 --> 00:23:53,140
It's the thing that motivates us to say no to sin and say yes to sacrificial serving.

268
00:23:53,140 --> 00:24:01,880
It's the thing that motivates us to live into this hard vision of community with brothers and sisters that all come from different places but all surrender to Jesus.

269
00:24:01,880 --> 00:24:04,060
It's hard.

270
00:24:04,060 --> 00:24:08,980
But we do it because we've been adopted into a new family.

271
00:24:08,980 --> 00:24:16,660
I'm really tempted to quote Lilo and Stitch, but it's been a while since I've seen it, and I don't want to butcher it.

272
00:24:16,660 --> 00:24:20,480
Yeah, it means family, right?

273
00:24:21,060 --> 00:24:22,940
We're brought into God's family.

274
00:24:22,940 --> 00:24:27,380
Whether or not we like the person that God decided to bring into our family or not, they're family.

275
00:24:27,380 --> 00:24:31,080
Brothers and sisters, mothers and fathers.

276
00:24:31,080 --> 00:24:36,580
So we've got to understand this.

277
00:24:36,580 --> 00:24:40,920
It's God's adoption of us as daughters and sons that teaches us obedience.

278
00:24:40,920 --> 00:24:43,220
And Paul says here it's a two-fold obedience.

279
00:24:43,360 --> 00:24:59,620
It's both saying no to sinful things that distract and harm us, and it's saying yes to hard things like community and sacrificial service that ultimately lead us to the life and flourishing that Jesus has invited us into.

280
00:24:59,620 --> 00:25:03,160
And I think this is where we can, both parties can miss it.

281
00:25:04,040 --> 00:25:11,800
I think it's really easy for religious people to say no to sin, easier, or at least the appearance of saying no to sin.

282
00:25:14,360 --> 00:25:17,180
But not saying yes to hard obedience.

283
00:25:17,180 --> 00:25:22,720
And it's easier for people who are just living in the world, not worried about sin.

284
00:25:22,720 --> 00:25:25,420
I'll do whatever I want to sacrificially serve those around them.

285
00:25:25,980 --> 00:25:31,780
But it's both of these things that need to happen in order for true obedience to happen.

286
00:25:31,780 --> 00:25:34,820
You can't do one or the other and say you're being obedient to Jesus.

287
00:25:34,820 --> 00:25:38,600
Obedience to Jesus requires both.

288
00:25:38,600 --> 00:25:41,220
And again, I use the word alignment because it started with an A.

289
00:25:41,220 --> 00:25:45,720
But what I'm really getting at here is identity-based obedience.

290
00:25:47,100 --> 00:25:59,940
That our identity as an adopted daughter or Son of God is the thing that changes our mindset, changes the way that we think about the world around us, and allows us to begin to obey hard things.

291
00:25:59,940 --> 00:26:04,940
Say no to sin and say yes to sacrificial obedience.

292
00:26:04,940 --> 00:26:09,660
We don't say no to sin and yes to God out of fear of judgment.

293
00:26:09,660 --> 00:26:13,860
Abba in heaven loves you.

294
00:26:15,420 --> 00:26:17,540
You don't need to prove to him anything.

295
00:26:17,540 --> 00:26:21,300
You don't obey out of a fear of being judged by God.

296
00:26:21,300 --> 00:26:23,040
You obey because he loves you.

297
00:26:23,040 --> 00:26:31,120
And you don't obey to try and earn some kind of extra favor with God, looking to your left and to your right, saying, God, you see me versus them?

298
00:26:31,120 --> 00:26:33,480
Don't you love me more than you love them?

299
00:26:33,480 --> 00:26:33,920
No.

300
00:26:33,920 --> 00:26:39,540
We don't do it to earn favor with God.

301
00:26:39,540 --> 00:26:41,660
We don't do it to avoid judgment from God.

302
00:26:41,660 --> 00:26:43,680
We do it because of who we are.

303
00:26:44,400 --> 00:26:46,100
We're no longer orphans on the run.

304
00:26:46,100 --> 00:26:50,840
We don't need to earn love from other things outside the world.

305
00:26:50,840 --> 00:26:56,100
We've been given it freely by the God who created us and who has all the love in the world to give.

306
00:26:58,020 --> 00:27:01,680
We no longer need to use his stuff to meet our fleshly desires.

307
00:27:01,680 --> 00:27:10,420
We are adopted children, heirs of the kingdom, and our brother is Christ who has shown us how to align our lives to the will of the Father in this present age.

308
00:27:10,420 --> 00:27:11,920
He is our example.

309
00:27:13,360 --> 00:27:14,860
And we practice obedience because it's who we are.

310
00:27:14,860 --> 00:27:16,880
And we practice obedience because it's who we are.

311
00:27:16,880 --> 00:27:21,540
James Clear, New Testament.

312
00:27:21,540 --> 00:27:26,160
See, when you go to Bible college, your head does weird stuff.

313
00:27:26,860 --> 00:27:28,980
And I abbreviate it in New York.

314
00:27:28,980 --> 00:27:30,640
And anyway.

315
00:27:30,640 --> 00:27:36,360
When you go to Bible college, every time you type the word his, you capitalize it.

316
00:27:36,360 --> 00:27:38,420
It just happens.

317
00:27:38,420 --> 00:27:40,040
Every time I'm like, that's not about Jesus.

318
00:27:40,040 --> 00:27:41,080
Don't capitalize it.

319
00:27:41,080 --> 00:27:43,920
I'd be like, Corey and his truck.

320
00:27:43,940 --> 00:27:46,360
And now all of a sudden, Corey's divinity in my email.

321
00:27:46,360 --> 00:27:48,500
All right.

322
00:27:48,500 --> 00:27:48,980
Sorry.

323
00:27:48,980 --> 00:27:53,400
James Clear, in his New York Times bestselling book, Atomic Habits.

324
00:27:53,400 --> 00:27:53,980
Anybody read it?

325
00:27:53,980 --> 00:27:55,760
A couple people.

326
00:27:55,760 --> 00:27:57,840
Very popular book for a long time.

327
00:27:57,840 --> 00:28:00,840
He makes the same argument from behavioral psychology.

328
00:28:00,840 --> 00:28:07,920
He talks about identity-based habits and how they're far more effective than outcome or process-based habits.

329
00:28:07,920 --> 00:28:13,140
The outcome-based habit says, I want to run a marathon, therefore, I need to run every day.

330
00:28:13,560 --> 00:28:17,760
It's like, I have this outcome in mind, and so I have to create these habits that lead me to this outcome.

331
00:28:17,760 --> 00:28:24,620
Process-based habits are, this is my training plan that I need to stick to in order to run a marathon.

332
00:28:24,620 --> 00:28:31,760
So I'm creating this plan, and I have to stick to it because it's the process that's going to be required of me to run a marathon.

333
00:28:31,760 --> 00:28:36,980
And then lastly, identity-based habits are, I'm a runner, so I run.

334
00:28:36,980 --> 00:28:42,100
And this is what we're getting at with discipleship to Jesus.

335
00:28:42,280 --> 00:28:44,300
I am a child of God.

336
00:28:44,300 --> 00:28:52,780
And so I live into community with my brothers and sisters in Christ, even when it's hard, and even when it requires hard conversations about difficult things.

337
00:28:52,780 --> 00:28:57,960
I do it because they are my brother, and they are my sister, and they are my father, and they are my mother in the faith.

338
00:28:57,960 --> 00:28:59,040
It is our identity.

339
00:29:00,480 --> 00:29:09,220
And I sacrificially serve others because I know that those outside the family of God are desperately hurting their orphans on the run from a God who loves them.

340
00:29:10,260 --> 00:29:16,500
And they have been grasping at every bit of creation they can to fill the void of that love that they have not felt.

341
00:29:16,500 --> 00:29:25,940
And it's me and us that have that love to take to them, and not to take it to them in a judgmental way, but to take it to them in a sacrificial way.

342
00:29:29,540 --> 00:29:32,160
It's identity-based obedience.

343
00:29:32,160 --> 00:29:36,920
And I'm trying this as a father, imperfectly as it might be.

344
00:29:36,920 --> 00:29:42,820
But in the Miller household, we are children of God.

345
00:29:43,400 --> 00:29:48,020
And so we align our lives with the values of the kingdom of God.

346
00:29:48,020 --> 00:29:52,540
One thing that we do on a regular daily basis with Rory is we pray the Lord's Prayer.

347
00:29:52,540 --> 00:29:57,040
We do it because this is the cry of the child of God.

348
00:29:57,040 --> 00:29:58,060
Your kingdom come.

349
00:29:58,060 --> 00:30:00,320
Your will be done on earth as it is in heaven.

350
00:30:00,320 --> 00:30:04,100
And then it goes on to talk about our participation in that.

351
00:30:04,100 --> 00:30:05,880
Lead us not into temptation.

352
00:30:05,880 --> 00:30:06,940
Deliver us from evil.

353
00:30:06,940 --> 00:30:07,720
Right?

354
00:30:09,060 --> 00:30:17,540
And the other day, Rory, over at the dinner table, he mentioned to us that his friend pushed him at daycare, which parent win, right?

355
00:30:17,540 --> 00:30:19,480
My kid told me something that happened at daycare.

356
00:30:19,480 --> 00:30:20,160
That's awesome.

357
00:30:20,160 --> 00:30:21,340
Praise the Lord.

358
00:30:21,340 --> 00:30:31,100
And so later that night, we're praying through the Lord's Prayer, and we get to that part, that statement, that we forgive those who sin against us.

359
00:30:31,100 --> 00:30:38,560
And I said, Rory, buddy, you forgive your friend that pushed you because God forgives you.

360
00:30:39,060 --> 00:30:39,880
It's identity.

361
00:30:39,880 --> 00:30:42,160
And he's two, and he has no clue what I'm saying.

362
00:30:42,160 --> 00:30:43,840
But we start now, right?

363
00:30:43,840 --> 00:30:44,760
We start now.

364
00:30:44,760 --> 00:30:45,940
It's identity.

365
00:30:45,940 --> 00:30:55,100
It's not you have to, or God's going to be mad at you, or you have to so God loves you more, or punch him back in the face next time because that's not right, right?

366
00:30:55,100 --> 00:30:57,960
All of us have probably done some version of all three of those parenting.

367
00:30:57,960 --> 00:31:03,260
But identity-based discipleship is we forgive because God has forgiven us.

368
00:31:03,260 --> 00:31:05,700
We serve because God has served us.

369
00:31:05,700 --> 00:31:08,240
We love because God has loved us.

370
00:31:09,780 --> 00:31:15,700
And there's going to come a point in Rory's life where he's going to have to decide if he wants to embrace that identity or not.

371
00:31:15,700 --> 00:31:17,920
I can't do that for him.

372
00:31:17,920 --> 00:31:24,540
But for those of us in the room that have already embraced our identity as followers of Jesus, it's not an option.

373
00:31:24,540 --> 00:31:25,400
It's our identity.

374
00:31:25,400 --> 00:31:26,920
It's who we are.

375
00:31:26,920 --> 00:31:28,380
We have to come into alignment.

376
00:31:28,380 --> 00:31:30,400
And this is a lifelong process, right?

377
00:31:30,400 --> 00:31:32,660
Thank you.

378
00:31:32,660 --> 00:31:34,440
This is a lifelong process.

379
00:31:35,140 --> 00:31:37,460
Sometimes it's two steps forward and three steps back.

380
00:31:37,460 --> 00:31:45,860
But the reality is we have, sometimes I think we take three steps back because we lose sight of identity and we move towards earning God's favor or running from his judgment.

381
00:31:47,420 --> 00:31:54,980
And if we're going to keep moving forward in obedience to Jesus' example, I think identity, alignment, obedience is what we need.

382
00:31:58,680 --> 00:32:00,580
And community, amen, whoever.

383
00:32:00,580 --> 00:32:02,560
Dave Ballinger's preaching better than me.

384
00:32:02,560 --> 00:32:03,020
Come on up.

385
00:32:03,020 --> 00:32:03,360
You want to?

386
00:32:03,360 --> 00:32:06,200
All right.

387
00:32:06,200 --> 00:32:07,360
Are we ready for our third A?

388
00:32:07,360 --> 00:32:09,280
We got adoption.

389
00:32:09,280 --> 00:32:10,480
We got alignment.

390
00:32:10,480 --> 00:32:11,880
And we have anticipation.

391
00:32:11,880 --> 00:32:14,440
Come on.

392
00:32:14,440 --> 00:32:16,380
Baptist preacher doing it this morning.

393
00:32:16,380 --> 00:32:17,000
Let's go.

394
00:32:17,000 --> 00:32:19,820
Baptist Bible grad 2014.

395
00:32:19,820 --> 00:32:20,620
You're welcome.

396
00:32:23,020 --> 00:32:23,500
All right.

397
00:32:23,500 --> 00:32:25,180
So, yeah, thanks, Mom and Dad.

398
00:32:25,180 --> 00:32:37,140
The adoption, the grace of God teaches us to come into alignment, obedience to Jesus, saying no to sin, saying yes to sacrificial service.

399
00:32:37,140 --> 00:32:46,940
Verse 13, while we wait for the blessed hope, the appearing of the glory of our great God and Savior, Jesus Christ.

400
00:32:46,940 --> 00:32:52,780
We live in a world that is still marred by sin.

401
00:32:52,860 --> 00:33:00,880
We are still awaiting Christ's ultimate arrival and fulfillment of all of the grace that he has promised to us and sealed for us in his resurrection.

402
00:33:00,880 --> 00:33:07,700
Aligning our lives with God's vision for humanity is hard because we live in a broken and rebellious world.

403
00:33:07,700 --> 00:33:20,980
But saying no to sin and yes to obedience gets a little bit easier when we have our eyes set to the future hope of Christ's return and him making all things new.

404
00:33:22,120 --> 00:33:31,040
Whether we realize it or not, all of creation is on a collision course for judgment or alignment with the will of the Father.

405
00:33:31,380 --> 00:33:35,520
And we've been invited to start this process early before Christ returns.

406
00:33:35,520 --> 00:33:36,140
We've been invited.

407
00:33:36,140 --> 00:33:46,860
That's what the Lord's Prayer is all about, that we as children of God are aligning ourselves with the will of God, with the kingdom of God, participating in his kingdom coming on earth as it is in heaven.

408
00:33:46,860 --> 00:33:53,440
Because one day, in the blink of an eye, whether we realize it or not, Christ will return and he will restore all things to himself.

409
00:33:53,440 --> 00:33:55,660
And so we get to participate in that early.

410
00:33:55,660 --> 00:33:56,220
Amen.

411
00:33:56,220 --> 00:33:58,560
We get to live into that in community.

412
00:33:58,560 --> 00:34:03,200
Now we get to go out to our brothers and sisters who have not said yes to that and invite them to do so.

413
00:34:03,280 --> 00:34:20,420
When we read some of the most encouraging passages of Scripture, like the wolf will lie down with the lamb and swords will be beaten into plowshares and every tear will be wiped from their eyes.

414
00:34:20,420 --> 00:34:27,940
As these truths are only possible because all of sin is finally dealt with once and for all.

415
00:34:27,940 --> 00:34:31,340
We're anticipating the day that that comes.

416
00:34:31,340 --> 00:34:36,740
And so for now, while we wait, we say no to sin and yes to obedience because we know that's where we're headed.

417
00:34:36,740 --> 00:34:45,200
All those who hold on to their rebellion against God with hard hearts will be judged or redeemed.

418
00:34:45,200 --> 00:34:50,000
All creation will be brought back into alignment with God's will for all eternity.

419
00:34:50,420 --> 00:34:57,460
We wait for the blessed hope, the appearing of the glory of our great God and Savior, Jesus Christ.

420
00:34:57,460 --> 00:35:05,500
